The frozen v101 actual-preflight auditor was never executed. Root's static
review found that it called `reader.sha` on a newly constructed but not yet
executed module. That method is absent until `exec_module` completes. The
v101 source bytes remain read-only as an unexecuted static NO_GO. The distinct
v102 auditor hashes the reader bytes with the standard library before loading
the module and additionally pins the actual transport-receipt JSON byte SHA.
It leaves the remaining receipt, source, command and chronology predicates
unchanged. No SSH or native action followed the v101 draft.
